// DistKV control-plane protocol — final design (v0.5).
//
// Two gRPC services replace the current ZMQ/JSON protocol:
//
//   - NodeServer: connector / plugin / agent <-> node CacheServer
//     (pool operations; plugins receive control-plane events via
//     HookService)
//   - CacheServerController: node server / PD worker <-> cluster controller
//     (membership, placement, global lookup, and PD rendezvous)
//
// Design principles
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Metadata only.  RPCs carry coordinates and metadata (node, pool,
//    offset, key, status).  Tensor bytes never travel over RPC; the data
//    plane reads/writes shm and RDMA directly.
// 2. Typed business outcomes.  ok / refused / not_found are carried in
//    ResponseHeader.status, NOT as gRPC status codes.  gRPC errors are
//    reserved for transport/protocol failures.
// 3. No transport-level request_id. gRPC correlates calls natively. The PD
//    request_id below is a business identity that binds one inference request
//    to a transfer session.
// 4. No ack flag.  Fire-and-forget COMMIT/RELEASE means "client does not
//    await the reply"; the server always replies at the transport level.
// 5. Layered geometry safety.  Hello (optional, recommended) validates
//    hma_signature against the pool's geometry; every segment carries
//    layout_signature as the per-operation backstop.  Either layer alone
//    prevents cross-geometry reads.
// 6. Connection setup is lazy.  shm name is deterministic
//    ("distkv-pool-{pool}"), size is available via fstat, and
//    shm_generation is echoed on every pool-scoped response — so pool ops
//    work without Hello.  Hello exists for early validation and config
//    delivery (persist policy, group id).
// 7. Plugin work is owned by the plugin.  The node server delivers
//    control-plane events to in-process plugins (the hook chain); a
//    plugin's data-plane work runs in its own daemon process, which is a
//    NodeServer client and receives commands over a plugin-private
//    protocol.

